# MLflow Parallel Training Bake-Off

## Project Overview

This project evaluates the performance difference between serial and parallel training of a fraud-detection model using **Scikit-learn and MLflow**.

The same `RandomForestClassifier` is trained twice: once using a single worker and once using all available CPU workers. MLflow tracks the training duration, worker configuration, and parallelization speedup for comparison.

## Objectives

- Compare serial and parallel model-training performance.
- Configure `RandomForestClassifier` to use one worker or all available CPU workers.
- Track experiment parameters and metrics with MLflow.
- Calculate the speedup achieved through parallel training.
- Save the trained model as a serialized pickle file.

